// leapfrog round 4 (after audit3): the only concept that films the skier from the FRONT. A 168 g glider (shared
// component table + 15 % margin) with a FEATHERED, span-morphing wing (tucked 0.55 m / 0.05 m² for fast flight and
// headwinds; feathers slide out to 1.0 m / 0.10 m² for slow flight, tailwinds, take-off and landing — LisHawk-style,
// Ajanic et al. 2020) is set down on the snow beside the skis and takes off by itself; it glides AHEAD of the skier on
// gravity (small pusher for take-offs and headwinds). Its tail pan/tilt camera (shared 4K 16:9 module, 22° lens) films the
// skier coming towards it; the output crop follows a LIVE tracker (NPU person detection + GNSS velocity feed-forward,
// modelled noise/latency/dropouts), not the true line of sight. Every wind gate runs on the shared windEstimate() with
// ≥5 s of history (the glider measures on the snow before take-off) and a robust error box; independent speed protection
// (anticipating throttle cut, feather air brake, crab, GNSS trim, altitude hold, land-now). Set-down and pick-up are
// simulated hand motions (MODAPTS, gloves); the wings fold themselves and the holster has a magnetic snap mouth.
// Physics: model.js; footage chain: analysis.js. 48-case ensemble (FULLRUN_CASES_R4): ensemble.js (generated by
// research/concepts_2026_10_19/dev/leapfrog/run_all.mjs). Numerical-uncalibrated simulation; nothing physically tested.
